# Lab Networking

- Every lab session receives a distinct network security boundary.
- Default lab egress is DENY for IPv4 and IPv6.
- Internet access requires an explicit named egress policy with minimum destinations/protocols.
- Labs cannot route to control-plane, management, metadata, link-local or other tenant networks.
- DNS uses a controlled resolver policy; arbitrary external resolvers are not implicitly permitted.
- Users never receive unrestricted runner management access.
- HTTP/WebSocket/terminal/SSH/RDP access is brokered through session-aware gateways.
- Gateway authorization validates authenticated user + active session + permitted endpoint; hostname knowledge alone is insufficient.
- Use short-lived connection tokens where practical.
- Production lab web origins use a different registrable domain from platform/authentication origins.
